    {
     "id": "chem170_scm_step601_infiltration",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run at chem_opt = 170 with Noah (sf_surface_physics = 2, num_soil_layers = 4, silt loam, dryland cropland, slopetyp 1), data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) kernels/noah_driver. Inputs are the dumped SFLX arguments (real32 values widened). The column is unfrozen and unsaturated at every dumped step, so the frozen-ground infiltration reduction fcr and SSTEP's supersaturation redistribution are UNTESTED, not merely unused, and so is every path that reads sice. INFILTRATION AND RUNOFF at afternoon, the heaviest rain of the set, canopy EXACTLY FULL so drip carries the whole canopy input and the storage limit binds. Reference at ESM_DT = 1e-4 s, which is NOT the smallest available and is chosen deliberately. WRF's infiltration limiter contains val = 1 - exp(-kdt dt/86400); as dt falls the argument underflows into the cancellation of 1 - exp(-x), and as dt rises val departs from its linear limit, so the replay's own accuracy is a V in dt. Measured on the step-601 column, the replay differs from this component by 5.8e-7 at dt = 1e-6, 1.1e-8 at dt = 1e-4 and 2.2e-5 at dt = 1, with a clean minimum at 1e-4; the runoff1 tolerance below is set from that floor and bounds the REFERENCE, not the component. runoff2 contains no dt-dependent quantity at all and is pinned at 1e-9.",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "edir": 30.678776706834583,
      "ec": 87.72652299304896,
      "etp": 175.45304598609786,
