     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run at chem_opt = 170 with Noah (sf_surface_physics = 2, num_soil_layers = 4, silt loam, dryland cropland, slopetyp 1), data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) kernels/noah_driver. Inputs are the dumped SFLX arguments (real32 values widened). The column is unfrozen and unsaturated at every dumped step, so the frozen-ground infiltration reduction fcr and SSTEP's supersaturation redistribution are UNTESTED, not merely unused, and so is every path that reads sice. INFILTRATION AND RUNOFF at second-day morning, peak evaporative demand, no rain. Reference at ESM_DT = 1e-4 s, which is NOT the smallest available and is chosen deliberately. WRF's infiltration limiter contains val = 1 - exp(-kdt dt/86400); as dt falls the argument underflows into the cancellation of 1 - exp(-x), and as dt rises val departs from its linear limit, so the replay's own accuracy is a V in dt. Measured on the step-601 column, the replay differs from this component by 5.8e-7 at dt = 1e-6, 1.1e-8 at dt = 1e-4 and 2.2e-5 at dt = 1, with a clean minimum at 1e-4; the runoff1 tolerance below is set from that floor and bounds the REFERENCE, not the component. runoff2 contains no dt-dependent quantity at all and is pinned at 1e-9.",
